        "claim": "rulesFiles does not de-duplicate paths. When CODEX_HOME equals the home directory, ~/AGENTS.md and <root>/AGENTS.md are the same file. On a case-insensitive filesystem, <root>/AGENTS.md and <root>/agents.md are also the same file. Each is then written, reported and checked twice. The install message says 'written' and then 'already current' for one file, and a file-level note ('Codex reads no file named agents.md') can be attached to a file that Codex does read. This is harmless to the bytes but misleading.",
